		{"id":"d4413463d5095026","type":"text","text":"## *Lesson F exercises 36-39*","x":-125,"y":290,"width":353,"height":50},
		{"id":"0607cb68c6521a63","type":"text","text":"- **Read the questions first:** Read the questions and answer options before you start so you know what information to listen for.\n- **Predict the topic:** Look at the title, pictures or introduction and think about which English words may appear.\n- **Recognise the purpose:** Ask yourself what kind of spoken text it is and what its purpose is.","x":-125,"y":366,"width":845,"height":175},
		{"id":"125583faf472e17d","type":"text","text":"**By the end of the lesson, students can understand the main idea and important details in a spoken text about a holiday and use listening strategies to find information.**","x":940,"y":66,"width":853,"height":101,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"c6b706cc76c9501b","type":"text","text":"I can: \n1. Predict what I am going to hear. \n2. Listen for the main idea and key details. \n3. Answer questions about *Holiday in Spain* using information from the audio.","x":940,"y":192,"width":787,"height":164,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5653c9c726347750","type":"text","text":"**Homework :Study Words F p.79 **","x":-115,"y":741,"width":290,"height":60,"color":"1"},
